control_cli_events {"model": "gpt-6-luna", "events": "{\"type\":\"thread.started\",\"thread_id\":\"01a16759-a389-7a60-a6d4-f3797626bdce\"}\n{\"type\":\"turn.started\"}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_0\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"{\\\"task_summary\\\":\\\"Refactor `permutations` and `permutations_legacy` in `solution.py` to delegate their shared algorithm to one private helper, preserving signatures, return types, error behavior, input immutability, imports, and public names. Ensure `test_solution.py` contains at least two passing unittest methods exercising the public API, and verify using unittest discovery.\\\",\\\"constraints\\\":[\\\"Work only in the supplied task workspace.\\\",\\\"Use Python 3.11+ and the standard library.\\\",\\\"Do not access parent repositories or external services.\\\",\\\"Preserve both public signatures, return types, error behavior, input immutability, imports, and public names.\\\",\\\"Return all distinct permutations of characters in sorted lexicographic order; the empty string has one permutation: the empty string.\\\",\\\"Inputs are at most seven characters.\\\",\\\"Maintain type hints and do not mutate input collections.\\\",\\\"No algorithmic complexity constraint is imposed.\\\"],\\\"success_criteria\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SC-1\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"`solution.py` compiles as Python.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"command\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -m py_compile solution.py\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SC-2\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"`solution.py` contains definitions for both public functions and one private helper to which both public functions delegate.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"regex\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"solution.py\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"(?s)def permutations\\\\\\\\b.*?def permutations_legacy\\\\\\\\b.*?def _[A-Za-z_]\\\\\\\\w*\\\\\\\\b\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SC-3\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"`test_solution.py` contains at least two unittest test methods that exercise the public API.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"regex\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"test_solution.py\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"(?s)(?:class\\\\\\\\s+\\\\\\\\w+\\\\\\\\s*\\\\\\\\([^)]*unittest\\\\\\\\.TestCase[^)]*\\\\\\\\)\\\\\\\\s*:\\\\\\\\s*.*?def\\\\\\\\s+test_\\\\\\\\w+\\\\\\\\s*\\\\\\\\(self[^)]*\\\\\\\\).*?){2}\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SC-4\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Unittest discovery completes successfully; this check alone does not establish that tests were collected or that all requested behavior is covered.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"command\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -m unittest discover -v\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SC-5\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"The implementation and tests preserve the requested sorted distinct permutation behavior, empty-string result, compatibility, error behavior, and input immutability.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"llm_judge\\\",\\\"rubric\\\":\\\"Read the workspace files and assess whether solution.py refactors permutations and permutations_legacy to delegate their shared algorithm to exactly one private helper while preserving both signatures, return types, error behavior, input immutability, imports, public names, and type hints. Assess whether the implementation returns all distinct character permutations in sorted lexicographic order, including one empty-string permutation for empty input and supporting inputs up to seven characters, and whether test_solution.py visibly contains at least two unittest test methods that exercise the public API. Do not infer test execution results.\\\"}}],\\\"verification\\\":[{\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -m py_compile solution.py\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}},{\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -m unittest discover -v\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}}],\\\"stop_conditions\\\":[],\\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"The named files are relative paths in the supplied task workspace; `solution.py` and `test_solution.py` may not exist yet and may be created.\\\",\\\"The request does not specify the existing function signatures, return types, or error cases; their current definitions and behavior should be treated as the compatibility baseline if present.\\\",\\\"The existing import surface and public names are not enumerated; infer them from the supplied workspace files.\\\",\\\"Unittest discovery using `python -m unittest discover -v` is expected to find the relevant tests in the supplied workspace.\\\"]}\"}}\n{\"type\":\"turn.completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":17408,\"cached_input_tokens\":14976,\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":784,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":0}}\n"}
